Z||000000||DJRice||07-09-99||07:16 AM||||Has anyone seen any software for the PC that can "talk to" or read the real-time data from the cars ECM?  It would seem to me that someone has done this but I havent seen anything like it on the net.
Z||000001||theogre||07-09-99||10:18 PM||||Yes, such things exist. You also need special hardware. The software can be had for free, or nearly so, but the hardware must be hand built<p>My choice of tool it the Auto Xray GM ECM scanner. 150$us. It plugs right in, and checks anything the ECM is capable of telling you. It works for all GM cars from 85 to 93-5. Auto Xray is available from a number of autoparts dealers, but Not Pep boys or Advance Auto. (I got mine at Strauss Discount Auto.)<p>There is a design issue with some GM ECM's. This issue applies to ALL methods of real time scanning. The problem is that the ECM CPU and programming can't handle doing 2 things at once in some ECMs. If idle speed changes while scanning, the car should not be driven and scanned. Again, this issue applies to ALL methods of real time scanning.
